There's a program called 'expect' (available at least for Unix systems)
that can create "keystrokes" for a program, depending on the the programs
"response".

> Operating system is Windows XP if it makes a difference.

That may make a difference, dunno.

There's also the possibility to use coprocesses (e.g. a kornshell feature;
kornshell is also available for WinDOS platforms) communicating through
pipes.

The hard part of your pseudocode, actually, may be the "process output",
and the actions to be derived from the parsing process. It might be quite
simple as long as you just want to automatize certain situations, but it
surely gets hard if you intend to create a Nethack-O-Matic expert system.

